  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a714.3 L961; \u00a79.3 L713\u2013L715; \u00a79.3 L702",
  "derivation": "Derived from the JS lot-4 seal (seal.json SHA-256 5d50127e5eac2791d4699f6cf4094b803bd05c1681a445298bf74a06b892f2c0), case file SHA-256 e36dc310694a3093737681f688da608764a3a1c056fb8e7f0238926022301a6d, by parity-sync decision PS-06 (DESIGN \u00a79.4 L723: IO object centres on one row line; RH = max(minHeight, max(object.h + label.h) + 2\u00b7padding), A = max(object.h/2), B = max(object.h/2 + label.h), cy = body.y + max(A, (RH + A \u2212 B)/2), object y = cy \u2212 h/2, one roundEven per coordinate): the input layout is the PS-06 layout of layout-009-grid-successor (side row on Z-page (padding 8, minHeight 40): Task_A (a-first, 100000x80000, no label) and Task_B (z-last, 100000x80000, label height 14000); Task_A y 7008 \u2192 8); R copies the layout geometry, so the Task_A occurrence y becomes 8, binding.layoutDigest = H(layout) and binding.payloadDigest = H({pages, occurrences, coverage, diagnostics}) are recomputed; nothing else changes. The JS seal carries the decided values. Values owned by that seal (harmonization \u00a73; parity sync PS-H18). JS derivation: R of the explicitly bound grid successor: the two side-stripe layout records are styled by their declaration (fill #eeeeff over plain, glyph aid = header-band, label Auxiliary); the aid label is the upper-cased stripped note text HELPER; associations are not laid out and stay nonvisual. Fails against: Dropping the stripe records, styling them as semantic occurrences, or recomputing their geometry in R.",
